import{_ as n,o as t,c as i,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 979 | Permanent Anti-Civilizational-Regression Mechanism · Mechanism 12 | Transcendent One's Perpetual-Motion Construction Duty","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 979 | Permanent Anti-Civilizational-Regression Mechanism · Mechanism 12 | Transcendent One's Perpetual-Motion Construction Duty","no":979,"module":5,"tags":["Anti-Regression","Mechanism 12","Transcendent One","Perpetual-Motion Construction","Anti-AFK"],"related":["919-Transcendent One's Perpetual-Motion Construction Duty","904-Collective-Ascension Duty","95-Key Figures and Organizations"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0979_模块5-机制十二-超脱者永动建设义务.md","filePath":"en/0979_模块5-机制十二-超脱者永动建设义务.md"}`),a={name:"en/0979_模块5-机制十二-超脱者永动建设义务.md"};function r(s,e,l,c,d,h){return t(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-979-permanent-anti-civilizational-regression-mechanism-·-mechanism-12-transcendent-one-s-perpetual-motion-construction-duty" tabindex="-1">Entry 979 | Permanent Anti-Civilizational-Regression Mechanism · Mechanism 12 | Transcendent One&#39;s Perpetual-Motion Construction Duty <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-979-permanent-anti-civilizational-regression-mechanism-·-mechanism-12-transcendent-one-s-perpetual-motion-construction-duty" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 979 | Permanent Anti-Civilizational-Regression Mechanism · Mechanism 12 | Transcendent One&#39;s Perpetual-Motion Construction Duty&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 5 · Civilization Final-Finalization Canonical Entries | Benchmark base: Documents 919, 904, 03</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-true-transcendence-is-not-hiding-away-for-retirement" tabindex="-1">Introduction: true transcendence is not hiding away for retirement <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-true-transcendence-is-not-hiding-away-for-retirement" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: true transcendence is not hiding away for retirement&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The most common regression across Myriad Heavens and Myriad Worlds is that once the strong transcend, they &quot;AFK&quot;: finding a cosmic corner to seclude, leaving Myriad Ranks to struggle on their own. The Anchor Symbiotic Civilization rejects this kind of transcendence by definition. The transcendent one&#39;s perpetual-motion construction duty is the anti-regression system&#39;s lock that &quot;prevents the strong from running away.&quot; Its logic under the six top-level axioms: the anti-predation axiom requires transcendence not by fleeing; the republican axiom of Myriad Races requires the strong have a beginning and an end with Myriad Ranks; the collective-ascension axiom explicitly says &quot;the strong do not ascend alone, but lift Myriad Ranks along&quot;; the causal self-discipline axiom requires the transcendent one&#39;s every step still be traceable; the law-first axiom requires the transcendence definition never retcon; the universal equal infinite law draws the transcendent one&#39;s responsibility — you have superimposed infinitely more layers of infinity than Myriad Ranks, so you have a duty to let this extra infinity continue flowing back to Myriad Ranks, rather than tucking away your infinity and roaming free. The old cosmos treats transcendence as retirement; the Anchor Symbiotic treats transcendence as a perpetual-motion post.</p><h2 id="i-mechanism-content" tabindex="-1">I. Mechanism Content <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-mechanism-content" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Mechanism Content&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Mechanism 12 stipulates: all beings reaching the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm and becoming transcendent ones automatically bear the perpetual-motion construction duty — no AFK seclusion, no running off to hermitage, no extracting their infinity from the Alaya Network. Transcendent ones must continuously bear construction duties: as mentors, as engineering heads, as law guardians, or as Youth-Supreme nurturers; specific posts are negotiated by the Council and the individual, not forced into a single trade.</p><h2 id="ii-operation" tabindex="-1">II. Operation <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-operation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Operation&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Perpetual-motion construction runs by post rotation:</p><ol><li><strong>Mentor post</strong>: in the Quest Sediment Domain mentoring Youth Supremes and new clans;</li><li><strong>Engineering post</strong>: leading hyper-multiverse-level methods, materials, and rules&#39; infinite iteration;</li><li><strong>Law post</strong>: maintaining the law network, calibrating setting self-consistency;</li><li><strong>Guardian post</strong>: guarding borders, defending against predation faction and Dark Substitution Body infiltration.</li></ol><p>Posts rotate every epoch; transcendent ones may not long monopolize some post, nor refuse a post.</p><h2 id="iii-anti-regression-principle" tabindex="-1">III. Anti-Regression Principle <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-anti-regression-principle" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Anti-Regression Principle&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Strong-one-AFK regression is civilization&#39;s highest-grade illness: the strongest batch runs off, and the remaining Myriad Ranks slowly lose direction. This mechanism&#39;s defense points:</p><ul><li><strong>Transcendence means taking a post</strong>: transcendence is not an endpoint, but a higher-intensity construction starting point;</li><li><strong>Post rotation</strong>: eliminating some transcendent one turning some post into private domain;</li><li><strong>Echoing Axiom 6</strong>: the higher the transcendent one superimposes, the more he feeds back; the easygoing mortals&#39; basic infinity partly comes from this feedback.</li></ul><p>Old-cosmos transcendent ones &quot;leap beyond the Three Realms, outside the Five Elements,&quot; and leave once and for all; Anchor Symbiotic transcendent ones &quot;leap beyond the Three Realms, and come back to mend roads.&quot;</p><h2 id="iv-supervising-subjects" tabindex="-1">IV. Supervising Subjects <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-supervising-subjects" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Supervising Subjects&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Transcendent ones&#39; duty performance is under Mechanism 7&#39;s four-dimensional assessment, Mechanism 1&#39;s tracing, and Mechanism 4&#39;s audit; those refusing posts, AFKing, or running off have their extra infinity-use tier-reclaimed per the collective-ascension axiom, retaining only basic infinity equal to all beings. Post allocation is legislated by the Council, and disputes adjudicated by the Symbiotic Court.</p><h2 id="appendix-a-concrete-scenario-—-a-transcendent-one-wants-a-small-universe-to-rest" tabindex="-1">Appendix: A Concrete Scenario — A Transcendent One Wants &quot;a Small Universe to Rest&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#appendix-a-concrete-scenario-—-a-transcendent-one-wants-a-small-universe-to-rest" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Appendix: A Concrete Scenario — A Transcendent One Wants &quot;a Small Universe to Rest&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A newly Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm transcendent one petitions the Council: he wants to apply for an undeveloped small universe for secluded quiet rest, no longer holding a public post. The Council replies per the perpetual-motion construction duty: you may change posts and may rest, but may not AFK-seclude nor extract from the network. He is finally assigned to the Quest Sediment Domain mentor post, for one epoch — no fighting and killing, just mentoring Youth Supremes. He is at first a little disappointed, but one epoch later he finds: the three Youth Supremes he mentored later all became construction backbones, and he himself in mentoring has a deeper layer of understanding of law. The old cosmos treats transcendence as retirement, the more transcendent the lonelier; the Anchor Symbiotic treats transcendence as a perpetual-motion post, the more transcendent the more to do, and the more needed by Myriad Ranks.</p><h2 id="vi-deleting-the-concept-of-retirement-from-civilization" tabindex="-1">VI: Deleting the Concept of &quot;Retirement&quot; from Civilization <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-deleting-the-concept-of-retirement-from-civilization" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI: Deleting the Concept of &quot;Retirement&quot; from Civilization&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The transcendent one&#39;s perpetual-motion construction duty is essentially redefining the endpoint. The old cosmos sets cultivation&#39;s endpoint as &quot;can stop working&quot; — so everyone&#39;s ultimate dream is finding a place to flat-lay. This setting looks beautiful, but actually bets civilization&#39;s future on the impossible premise that &quot;the strong all want to lie down.&quot; The Anchor Symbiotic changes this endpoint to &quot;always something to do, the more done the more interesting.&quot; Transcendent ones are no longer retired elders, but civilization&#39;s most senior builders. Deleting the concept of &quot;retirement,&quot; civilization forever has the strongest batch on the job. This is not hard labor, but gives the transcendent one a more fulfilling position than roaming alone — being needed by Myriad Ranks is itself a higher infinity.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: directing transcendent ones&#39; massive energy toward perpetual-motion construction, eliminating great-material-for-small-use AFK retirement</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: transcendent ones may not extract from the network to roam alone, their power always serving Myriad Ranks</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo-type heavenly emperors after cultivation flat-lay, with Myriad Ranks as backdrop; Heng Yuan Zhou transcendent ones perpetually construct, the more transcendent the more to work</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: transcendent ones&#39; mentor and guardian posts directly face all Myriad-Rank beings</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: transcendent ones&#39; engineering posts iterate infinitely with the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm&#39;s expansion, with no retirement line</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The transcendent one&#39;s perpetual-motion construction duty rewrites &quot;transcendence&quot; from flight into responsibility. As long as the strongest forever construct, civilization never loses its leader — and regression loses its most fatal exit of &quot;the strong run off.&quot;</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/919_模块5-第十八条-超脱者永动建设义务.html">Entry 919 · Transcendent One&#39;s Perpetual-Motion Construction Duty</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/904_模块5-第三条-集体升维义务.html">Entry 904 · Collective-Ascension Duty</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/978_模块5-机制十一-文明权重评估制.html">Entry 978 · Mechanism 11</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',26)])])}const p=n(a,[["render",r]]);export{m as __pageData,p as default};
